 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "ArticleSystem() starts empty. addArticle(articleName) gives the next id (1, 2, ...) to a new article with score 0 and returns it. upvoteArticle(articleId, userId): no effect when the user already upvoted the article; otherwise the user's vote becomes an upvote, the score rises by 1 (by 2 when it replaces a downvote) and replacing a downvote records a flip. downvoteArticle(articleId, userId) mirrors this. getRecentFlips(userId, k) returns the names of up to k distinct articles the user has flipped, most recent flip first (an article flipped again moves to the front). getTopArticles(k) returns the names of up to k articles by score descending, ties by smaller id. Ids passed to votes always exist. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk15-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
